# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, whatever a contributor's editor writes is what lands. #734 was
# authored with CRLF and five files came across converted, one of them
# app/api/v1/endpoints/paddle_webhook.py; the churn buried a 56-line test change
# under a 2,482-line diff in test_deep_features_10_12.py and made `git blame`
# on those files useless before that commit.
#
# text=auto leaves binaries alone: git detects them by content, so the 300-odd
# tracked fonts and images under .scratch/ are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Force LF line endings for shell scripts (required for Linux containers)
*.sh text eol=lf
# Dockerfile* so variants are covered too (Dockerfile.postgres): a CRLF
# checkout breaks the backslash line continuations inside RUN.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
